<title>PAKISTAN: Sixteen killed in Pakistani rainstorms.</title>
<headline>Sixteen killed in Pakistani rainstorms.</headline>
<dateline>MUZAFFARABAD, Pakistan 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least 16 people were killed by lightning and rainstorms in Pakistan-ruled Kashmir overnight, state police said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said eight people were killed by lightning in a village northeast of the state capital Muzaffarabad and another eight were swept away by flash floods caused by heavy rains in the area.</p>
<p>Widespread rains over the past few days have also flooded low-lying areas in Pakistan's central province of Punjab, government officials said.</p>
